st handling of potential authentication issues. I'm getting close.\n\n\n**Constructing the Script**\n\nI am now structuring the entire push process into a single PowerShell script to fulfill the batch requirement. I'm focusing on directly implementing the core actions: cloning or pulling the repository, creating the target session directory, and copying relevant files. I'm using the `ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'` setting to ensure any failure halts the process, aiding in debugging. I'm now drafting the script with the user-provided parameters to implement a complete, single-execution flow.\n\n\n**Implementing File Operations**\n\nI'm now writing the PowerShell script to handle file operations. I'm focusing on creating directories for transcripts and tasks, and then copying the relevant files recursively. This includes handling the session summary Markdown file and incorporating the session ID, to ensure all artifacts are in the correct place. I'm building it up, step by step.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Push Script**\n\nI'm now integrating the generated artifacts, the session summaries and analyses, into the workflow. I'm focusing on incorporating the final `git push` commands. I'm making it easier for me to use the script by simplifying the authentication. Finally, I've added a note to handle potential branch name inconsistencies between `main` and `master`, which can sometimes pop up. This is the last task before the final execution!\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$script = @'\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'\n$repoUrl = \"https://github.com/pp0016/daily-push.git\"\n$brainDir = \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\294de91b-96ee-4dd8-a251-293eb7aa59a8\"\n$scratchDir = \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\"\n$repoDir = Join-Path $scratchDir \"daily-push\"\n$sessionDir = Join-Path $repoDir \"sessions\\294de91b-96ee-4dd8-a251-293eb7aa59a8\"\n\nWrite-Host \"Cloning or updating repo...\"\nif (Test-Path $repoDir